[carljm 2026-07-18] I am not sure that we are gaining anything by being more conservative about applying bound-method descriptor semantics to callable types, and using more limited heuristics (like dunder-name), vs just fully matching mypy/pyright behavior. There is no "always right" answer here, and by choosing a different "sometimes right" answer than the two most widely used type checkers, it seems like we mostly just create pain for users.
