################ issue astral-sh/ty#4054
#4054 [OPEN] Missing diagnostic for unpacking multiple TypeVarTuples in non-`tuple` generics
author: MeGaGiGaGon  created: 2026-07-21T18:32:22Z  closed: null
labels: bug,diagnostics,generics,typing semantics,variadic-generics
--- body
### Summary

Classes and type aliases are missing the diagnostic for unpacking multiple TypeVarTuples at the same time (though the fallback to `tuple[object, ...]` still works)
https://play.ty.dev/5346e13f-abe9-4656-91b0-1416cff0f254
```py
from typing import reveal_type

# Error: Multiple unpacked variadic tuples are not allowed in a `tuple` specialization 
def works_as_expected[*TS1, *TS2](x: tuple[*TS1, *TS2]):
    reveal_type(x)  # Revealed type: `tuple[object, ...]` 

class A[*TS]: ...
type B[*TS] = tuple[*TS]

# No error on `a` or `b`
def doesnt_work[*TS1, *TS2](a: A[*TS1, *TS2], b: B[*TS1, *TS2]):
    reveal_type(a)  # Revealed type: `A[*tuple[object, ...]]` 
    reveal_type(b)  # Revealed type: `tuple[object, ...]` 
```

### Version

ty 0.0.61 (56b2c24 2026-07-17) playground 5e698d5e4
